  "description_text": "This page includes rechargeable lithium batteries and matching chargers designed for portable devices and DIY builds. With multiple voltage and capacity options, it provides dependable power for applications such as model toys, small robots, lighting setups, and other battery-powered projects. To ensure safe and efficient charging, please choose the correct charger for the selected battery model.\n\nMultiple Options Includes two battery models and two charger models for different power needs. Rechargeable Power Designed for repeated use in portable electronic devices and DIY applications. Practical for DIY Builds Suitable for portable electronics, lighting kits, remote projects, and custom builds.\n\nMultiple Options Includes two battery models and two charger models for different power needs.\n\nRechargeable Power Designed for repeated use in portable electronic devices and DIY applications.\n\nPractical for DIY Builds Suitable for portable electronics, lighting kits, remote projects, and custom builds.\n\nThis product utilizes a replaceable rechargeable lithium battery.\n\nAdult supervision is required when children are handling batteries or the charger. Do not operate the product while it is charging.\n\nEnsure the battery is installed correctly. Improper installation may result in short circuits, overheating, or potential explosion.\n\nRegularly inspect the charger’s cord, plug, housing, and other components for damage. If any damage is found, discontinue use immediately until the device is fully repaired.\n\nChoking Hazard: Contains small parts; not suitable for children under 3 years of age.\n\nImproper disposal of this product may harm the environment - please recycle responsibly.\n\nUse only the officially supplied charger. The charger is not a toy.\n\nUse a standard 5V DC power source with at least 2A output. A 5V/2A USB power adapter is recommended for proper charging performance.\n\nDO NOT use power adapters with output voltage higher than 5V, or adapters that may trigger 9V/12V fast-charging modes, as this may cause device damage, overheating, or fire hazards.\n\nCharging from some computer USB ports may be slow or may not provide sufficient current for normal charging.\n\nDO NOT cover the device while charging, and keep it away from high temperature, humidity, or flammable environments. Never charge the device unattended.\n\nDO NOT charge the battery pack if it is overheating. Allow it to cool down completely before recharging.\n\nIf the battery pack or charger becomes wet, ensure they are thoroughly dry before attempting to charge.\n\nDO NOT attempt to use or charge the battery pack if it shows any signs of leakage or corrosion.\n\nDO NOT disassemble, crush, or mechanically abuse the battery pack.\n\nDO NOT dispose of the battery pack in fire.\n\nExercise extreme caution when handling an overheated battery pack.",
